💡 **SUGGESTION: extract the bounded backstop-wait idiom into a tiny helper — it now exists 4× in this file**

Leg 3 correctly added the bounded backstop-wait to both never-started signal tests (`cancelled-111` at ~line 864, `cancelled-777` at ~line 1016), but the identical 5-line idiom — deadline + 50 ms artifact-poll loop — now appears four times in this file:

1. the parse-loss never-started test (`cancelled-888`, ~line 1083)
2. the TERM never-started test (`cancelled-111`, line 864)
3. the INT never-started test (`cancelled-777`, line 1016)
4. (and the same deadline/`while` shape again in `waitForLog`/`waitForPolls` at lines 355/377)

A 6-line `DwLive` helper would collapse the three artifact polls and make the next death-shape fix a one-line change instead of three:

```dart
/// Waits (bounded) for the detached backstop's cancel artifact to land —
/// the cancel is asynchronous by design on the poisoned-parse death shape.
Future<void> waitForCancel(DwLive live, int runId) async {
  final deadline = DateTime.now().add(const Duration(seconds: 10));
  while (DateTime.now().isBefore(deadline)) {
    if (File('${live.dir.path}/cancelled-$runId').existsSync()) return;
    await Future<void>.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 50));
  }
}
```

Call sites become `await live.waitForCancel(111); expect(File('…cancelled-111…').existsSync(), isTrue, …);`. Non-blocking — behavior is identical; pure consolidation, follow-up friendly.

